From 7fa07dd65b2c8ac2d4713cf555f9c5f0681440a9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 11 Jul 2026 11:37:23 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 08/28] base: contain the AROS GLOBAL qualifier

AI_PHASE: chromium-headless-phase-3

AI_STATUS: complete

ROOT_CAUSE: exec/types.h exports GLOBAL as the legacy extern storage qualifier, which rewrote V8's RegExpMacroAssembler::GLOBAL enum token and broke every downstream regexp declaration.

FIX_REASON: Remove GLOBAL at V8's internal macro boundary beside REGISTER; V8 does not consume the AROS qualifier and uses GLOBAL as owned C++ identity in both headers and sources.

SCOPE: src/base/macros.h

VALIDATION: ninja -C out/aros-headless -j16 obj/v8/v8_base_without_compiler/external-reference.o

RISK: low; the undef is AROS-only and applies after platform headers at V8's internal source boundary.

AI_DECISION_CHAIN: ACD-chromium-native-port-roadmap
---
 src/base/macros.h | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/base/macros.h b/src/base/macros.h
index ed0a1aa..9d837cb 100644
--- a/src/base/macros.h
+++ b/src/base/macros.h
@@ -13,8 +13,9 @@
 #include "src/base/logging.h"
 
 #if V8_OS_AROS
-// exec/types.h exposes this legacy storage qualifier in the global macro
-// namespace, where it collides with V8 register-location enum values.
+// exec/types.h exposes these legacy storage qualifiers in the global macro
+// namespace, where they collide with V8 enum values.
+#undef GLOBAL
 #undef REGISTER
 #endif
 
